Description: Add NC12 to mojo media client GetPreferredRenderableFourccs (Pi 5)
 PICKFMT_DIAG instrumentation (patch 0008) revealed that on Linux/Pi 5 the
 production VideoDecoderPipeline::Create() call site in
 media/mojo/services/gpu_mojo_media_client_linux.cc is fed by
 GetPreferredRenderableFourccs(), which builds its own fourccs list and never
 consults VideoDecoderPipeline::DefaultPreferredRenderableFourccs(). Patch 0004
 added NC12 to DefaultPreferredRenderableFourccs() but that function is only used
 by oop_video_decoder_factory_service.cc, which is not the path we hit.
 .
 Result observed in chromium-hevc.err:
 .
   [PICKFMT_DIAG] renderable_fourccs_ size=2 candidates size=1
   [PICKFMT_DIAG] renderable: AR24 v4l2=0x34325241
   [PICKFMT_DIAG] renderable: BGR4 v4l2=0x34524742
   [PICKFMT_DIAG] candidate:  NC12 v4l2=0x3231434e
   [PICKFMT_DIAG] NO MATCH after full scan
 .
 This patch injects Fourcc::NC12 at the front of GetPreferredRenderableFourccs's
 returned vector when BUILDFLAG(USE_V4L2_CODEC_RPI) is defined. Front position
 ensures NC12 wins the candidate-match loop in PickDecoderOutputFormat() over
 the trailing AR24 / BGR4, so the V4L2 stateless decoder's NC12 output is
 accepted as a renderable format and the decode pipeline proceeds.
 .
 Patch 0004 is left in place (harmless; provides correctness for the in-process
 OOP factory path on the off chance we ever route through it).
Author: agora <build@agora>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-05-03
--- a/media/mojo/services/gpu_mojo_media_client_linux.cc
+++ b/media/mojo/services/gpu_mojo_media_client_linux.cc
@@ -48,6 +48,15 @@ std::vector<Fourcc> GetPreferredRenderableFourccs(
     const gpu::GpuPreferences& gpu_preferences,
     const gpu::GpuFeatureInfo& gpu_feature_info) {
   std::vector<Fourcc> renderable_fourccs;
+#if BUILDFLAG(USE_V4L2_CODEC_RPI)
+  // EXPERIMENTAL: Pi 5 BCM2712 column-tiled NV12 (NC12) from rpi-hevc-dec
+  // /dev/video19. Inserted first so PickRenderableFourcc()/
+  // PickDecoderOutputFormat() prefer it over the trailing AR24/BGR4
+  // 1-copy/conversion paths. Without this, V4L2VideoDecoder fails with
+  // "Failed to pick an output format" because its only candidate (NC12)
+  // is not in renderable_fourccs_. See patches/0008-pickfmt-diag.patch.
+  renderable_fourccs.emplace_back(Fourcc::NC12);
+#endif
 #if BUILDFLAG(ENABLE_VULKAN)
   // Support for zero-copy NV12/P010 textures preferentially.
   if (gpu_preferences.gr_context_type == gpu::GrContextType::kVulkan) {
